For the slope field of $\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\dfrac{x}{y}$:
(a) Sketch the solution curve through $(0,3)$.
(b) Verify that $y=\sqrt{x^2+9}$ is that solution.
Vertical marks on $y=0$ indicate undefined gradients; no element is assigned at the origin.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[color=black,->] (-3.6,0)--(3.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
